Package: predictVoterIdeologyR
Type: Package
Title: Predicting the Voter Ideology of Survey Respondents based on Random Forest Classification Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
person("Patrick", "Mellacher", role = c("aut", "cre")),
person("Gernot", "Lechner", role = "aut")
)
Description: This package reproduces the random forest classification framework developed in "Objectifying the Measurement of Voter Ideology With Expert Data" (Mellacher and Lechner, 2025) 
in R with a high accuracy (>98%) compared to the original Python implementation.

The package contains a function that takes a dataframe containing 6 key independent variables as input and returns the predicted position of the respondent on three ideology scales: 
general left-right, economic left-right and GAL-TAN (Green/Alternative/Libertarian - Traditional/Authoritarian/Nationalist.

Depends:
R (>= 4.2.0)
License: MIT
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
